#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:3 of
msgid ""
"Chaos-based modulator. Implements the "
":class:`~chaotic_pfc.comms.protocols.Transmitter` protocol — a callable "
"that embeds a message in the state of a Hénon oscillator."
msgstr ""
"Chaos-based modulator. Implements the "
":class:`~chaotic_pfc.comms.protocols.Transmitter` protocol — a callable "
"that embeds a message in the state of a Hénon oscillator."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:7 of
msgid "Two transmitters are provided, mirroring the two receiver modes:"
msgstr "Two transmitters are provided, mirroring the two receiver modes:"

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:9 of
msgid ""
":func:`transmit` — 2-D Hénon carrier. The message ``m[n]`` is added to "
"the state ``x₁[n]`` before it feeds back into the next iteration, so the "
"emitted carrier is"
msgstr ""
":func:`transmit` — 2-D Hénon carrier. The message ``m[n]`` is added to "
"the state ``x₁[n]`` before it feeds back into the next iteration, so the "
"emitted carrier is"

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:13 of
msgid "s[n] = x_1[n] + \\mu \\, m[n]"
msgstr "s[n] = x_1[n] + \\mu \\, m[n]"

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:17 of
msgid "and the updated state becomes ``x_1[n+1] = a - s[n]^2 + b \\, x_2[n]``."
msgstr "and the updated state becomes ``x_1[n+1] = a - s[n]^2 + b \\, x_2[n]``."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:20 of
msgid ""
":func:`transmit_order_n` — higher-order Hénon with an internal FIR filter"
" whose taps form the coefficient vector ``c``. The carrier is taken from "
"the filtered state component ``x[2][n]``."
msgstr ""
":func:`transmit_order_n` — higher-order Hénon with an internal FIR filter"
" whose taps form the coefficient vector ``c``. The carrier is taken from "
"the filtered state component ``x[2][n]``."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.transmitter:24 of
msgid ""
"Both functions are deterministic given their inputs. Where a random "
"initial condition is needed (``transmit_order_n`` with ``x0=None``), a "
"``seed`` parameter exposes the RNG so callers can reproduce results."
msgstr ""
"Both functions are deterministic given their inputs. Where a random "
"initial condition is needed (``transmit_order_n`` with ``x0=None``), a "
"``seed`` parameter exposes the RNG so callers can reproduce results."

